      "content": "If the climb was your reason for breathing, then the silence at the top is terrifyingly loud. It's a profound moment of freedom, even if it feels like an ending. You don't need a grand new purpose to justify staying; sometimes the most radical act is simply allowing yourself to *be* without having to earn it. Let go of the expectation that life must have a dramatic next act.",
